<title>GERMANY: Ford-Werke says aims for break-even in 97.</title>
<headline>Ford-Werke says aims for break-even in 97.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Ford-Werke AG, the German unit of U.S. carmaker Ford Motor Co, said on Thursday it was aiming to break even this year after reporting a loss of 551.6 million marks in 1996.</p>
<p>The company was aiming to hold sales steady and reach &quot;a neutral result&quot; in 1997, supervisory board chairman Albert Caspers said at the opening of a new Ford branch in Stuttgart.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope that we will end at break-even,&quot; Caspers said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
